      "problem": "What is the solution to the equation $0.9s=3.6?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.9s & =3.6 \\\\ 10\\cdot (0.9s) & =10\\cdot (3.6) \\\\ 9s & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9s & =36 \\\\ \\frac{9s}{9} & =\\frac{36}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{9}s}{\\cancel{9}} & =\\frac{36}{9} \\\\ s & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
